write_json('criteria.json',{'schema':'hug_criteria_classification_v1','scope':'Local documentary provenance only. External papers were not independently reread in this subtask.','items':criteria,'new_acceptance_thresholds':None,'historical_failures_reclassified':False,'new_geometry_queries':0,'physics_steps':0,'new_eval_data':False})
report=f'''# HUG mapping criteria provenance

15 October 2026. Read-only audit of local code, documentation, frozen protocols and six historical commits. No inference, geometry queries, fitting, physics or evaluation data were created. External-paper claims are reported here only as local attributions; the separate upstream-paper review must verify them.

**The checks are not a single HUG-paper validity standard.** They combine implementation correctness, project engineering safeguards and a deliberately strict geometric preservation claim. The latest nine strict failures remain failures under that claim. They do not establish that every useful approximate Shadow retargeter is impossible, nor that HUG failed its own benchmark.

| Item | Provenance and role | Limit |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Native reconstruction, frames, named joints, actual source limits and independent FK | Hard correctness checks for the declared conversion | Reproducing a wrist-to-palm convention does not prove anatomical or surface equivalence. |
| Mean tip error ≤10 mm | Engineering inference admission guard, introduced in `4f972f0` | Not a paper-derived native-to-Shadow fidelity tolerance; individual tips may still exceed 10 mm. |
| Bands at 1/2/5 mm | Earliest located full triple in `2d8e000`, explicitly diagnostic | Not simulator contact thresholds or empirically validated error budgets. |
| Zero lost/added relationships and no reliable sign reversals | Frozen project definition of strict native-relative preservation | Selecting this strong claim as necessary for useful prediction is a research choice, not a demonstrated necessity. |
| Each tip no worse than its original error | Added after average-loss fitting worsened individual fingers | Protects the particular baseline, whose absolute error can remain substantial. |
| Normal facing/away sign | Geometric hemisphere test with numerical and feature eligibility safeguards | Same sign can remain very oblique; no contact-force or continuous normal-field guarantee. |
| Per-part literal collider surfaces | Explicit measurement-reference choice | Includes buried collider interfaces for distance; differs from the exposed boundary and active contacts. |
| Original q ±0.35 rad | Experimental search trust region intersected with source physical bounds | Search design, not an accuracy margin or global feasibility certificate. |

## Evidence and chronology

The 10 mm guard first appears in the inspected history in commit `4f972f0` (6 October) as a configuration gate checked before normal inference proceeds to simulation. The saved patch contains no paper-derived numerical rationale for the value. The current {link('engineering_guard','static protocol')} explicitly calls it an engineering guard. Its error compares **mapped and native fingertips**, which is not fingertip-to-object distance.

The {link('earliest_located_bands','earliest located full triple-band protocol')} says `bands_are_acceptance_thresholds:false`. The {link('frozen_rule','later frozen rule')} carries the scales into a strict same-part relationship claim. Rule SHA-256 is `87da8d6c03c0f5692f08cbad99f3af42f72f16d818b5b30df581791361d400d4`. Freezing before reading the new reports protects against fitting this rule to those reports; it does not make the rule a universal scientific tolerance.

The {link('caps_historical_motivation','prior surface-fit decision')} records improvement in aggregate cost while tip/middle errors worsened in every case. The {link('caps_historical_adoption','subsequent constraint decision')} introduces per-tip original-error bounds. The earliest constrained version declared a 10 nm numerical allowance; the later {link('caps_later_literal','feasible solver')} uses literal baseline limits. These versions must not be merged into one historical claim. The present exact caps prevent further regression, not inherited baseline error.

The {link('trust_not_accuracy','original correction report')} explicitly says ±0.35 rad and the residual scaling are implementation choices, not acceptable mapping tolerances. Actual source joint limits are a different restriction. Failure of a finite optimizer within this trust region cannot prove that no Shadow pose can satisfy a geometric target.

The {link('papers_do_not_certify_choices','acceptance document')} explicitly states that papers motivate measurement structure but do not certify these acceptance choices. No local evidence inspected establishes the numerical values as HUG's required mapping standard.

## Geometry and evidence limitations

The {link('acceptance_contract','declared geometry contract')} compares distances to native open anatomical patches and literal individual collider surfaces. The {link('literal_boundary_implementation','implementation')} takes unsigned per-collider distances; the union of collider surfaces is not the boundary of their occupied union. Interior interfaces can therefore matter to this literal metric. The {link('normal_eligibility_and_sign','orientation implementation')} separately excludes buried closest points and unreliable features. Neither result is a direct measurement of accessible force-bearing contact, and overlapping anatomical masks must not be summed into physical contact area.

The {link('orientation_definition','normal-sign definition')} is geometrically interpretable, but matching signs only establishes agreement at eligible sites. Distance bounds do not bound discontinuous nearest-feature normals. Missing coverage stays unresolved. Making a previously failing relationship ambiguous is not evidence that it was repaired.

The {link('source_interval_code','cell interval code')} uses the 1-Lipschitz property of distance to a fixed set and triangle radii, conditional on the stated arithmetic allowance. The {link('identity_control_limit','already completed identity control')} shows that independent intervals can retain positive possible mismatch for identical fields that straddle a band. This is a certificate limitation, not actual geometry mismatch or invalidation of definite counterexamples. The {link('latest_unchanged_failure','latest completed study')} still records nine strict failures after all thirty original tip caps and six mean guards passed.

## Better-grounded next assessment

1. Name the intended claim first: predicting the outcome of an executed, declared Shadow retargeting pipeline differs from predicting what the native MANO proposal would have done. Source-to-robot distortion remains a potential confound for comparing generator diversity.
2. Retain source/FK/frame/physical-limit checks. Choose and document the reference geometry and anatomical correspondence explicitly, including rendered surface, individual colliders, exposed union boundary and simulator contact conventions. Do not silently replace the frozen domain.
3. Keep the current bands, continuous per-finger distances, normal evidence and penetration/miss descriptors as measurements. Do not choose a new margin just above current failures or borrow a paper's aggregate error as a pass limit.
4. If the goal remains universal equality, develop a separately versioned paired/feature-stability certificate to reduce conservative uncertainty. This cannot erase existing definite mismatches. If the goal is approximate Shadow adequacy, specify a new prospective, claim-specific protocol using externally justified error allowances or separate calibration evidence; no such value is established here.
5. For downstream adequacy, later authorized outcome-sensitivity tests under a fixed controller and held-out objects should quantify whether mapping distortions materially alter results. The repeatedly inspected cases are development evidence, not an independent test set. Preserve poor native proposals, refusals and mapper versions; successful lifting alone is not a mapping gate.

All of the above are recommendations, not a new operational acceptance policy. No thresholds, historical results, code or shared documentation were changed by this audit.

`evidence.json` binds 23 exact path/line excerpts, four protocol/control hashes, six commit identities and the original gate patch. `criteria.json` provides the structured classification. The review of the parent's clarification is separate and bound to its snapshot hashes.
'''
(OUT/'REPORT.md').write_text(report)
inputs=[]
for name in ['criteria_alignment.md','approximate_protocol_design.json']:
 p=Path('/private/tmp/hug_criteria_alignment_root_2026-10-15_v1')/name
 inputs.append({'path':str(p),'sha256':hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()})
review={'schema':'hug_criteria_alignment_local_provenance_review_v1','reviewed_inputs':inputs,'local_provenance_interpretation_passed':True,'external_paper_claims_independently_checked_here':False,'historical_results_reclassified':False,'blocking_findings':[],'comments':[{'severity':'precision','topic':'optimization domains','suggestion':'Replace fixed translation boxes with source-reach-derived translation boxes to distinguish their provenance from the chosen ±0.35rad trust region. Neither is a fidelity tolerance.'},{'severity':'scope','topic':'strong equivalence wording','suggestion':'The strong equivalence in the table refers only to the declared bands/sign states and complete coverage. It is not equality of all distances, full shape, force or task outcome. The remainder of the draft already makes this clear.'},{'severity':'evidence responsibility','topic':'upstream HUG paper and exporter','suggestion':'The local documentary claims are supported. Exact external paper/exporter facts should use the independent source review; this review did not open those sources.'}],'agrees_with':['10mm native-target guard distinct from HUG fingertip-to-object measure','strict nine failures retained','practical Shadow adequacy currently untested','literal collider surfaces distinct from exposed contacts','identity-control ambiguity does not undo definite witnesses','new thresholds remain null and future calibration remains prospective'],'new_geometry_queries':0,'new_eval_data':False}
write_json('root_draft_review.json',review)
write_json('preparation_history.json',{'events':[{'event':'Initial read-only evidence extraction aborted','cause':'Requested excerpt range exceeded 53-line acceptance rule file length; assertion stopped before writing evidence.json.','resolution':'Bound requested excerpt end to actual source length; stored range is actual. No scientific code, metrics, data or thresholds changed.'}],'scope':'Formatting and text extraction only'})
files=[]
for p in sorted(OUT.iterdir()):
 if p.is_file() and p.name!='manifest.json':files.append({'path':p.name,'size_bytes':p.stat().st_size,'sha256':hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest()})
write_json('manifest.json',{'schema':'hug_criteria_provenance_manifest_v1','created_utc':datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc).isoformat(),'files':files,'no_shared_edits':True,'no_new_eval_data':True})
print(json.dumps({'files':len(files),'manifest_sha256':hashlib.sha256((OUT/'manifest.json').read_bytes()).hexdigest(),'report':str(OUT/'REPORT.md')},indent=2))
